{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling: run the whole typecheck before each gate START.\n\nBoth NF-5 gate attempts ended before a test ran. Attempt 1 failed at\nthe helpers step in 1.9 s. Attempt 2 failed at typecheck in 12.7 s:\ntwo test files in packages/scope still call the removed custody API.\nThe checks of the affected compiler contexts did not cover them.\n\nFrom now, before a START act for a full gate, root runs two commands\nat the exact head, in the executor slot:\n\n1. node scripts/check-shared-helpers.mjs\n2. npm run typecheck\n\nBoth must exit 0. The START act states the two exit codes. The two\ncommands need no separate grant, no evidence directory and no END act.\nThey read the checkout and write no tracked file. The rule holds for\neach lane, and it holds for a retry after a repair.\n\nA change that removes or renames an export also gets one grep of the\nrepository for the old name before its commit. The grep covers test\ndirectories of every package.\n\nThe tooling head (GS-3 and FH-1) adds one sentence with this rule to\ndocs/testing.md, beside the gate record. FH-1's hook does not run the\ntypecheck, because it takes more than two seconds.\n\nNF-5: migrate the two callers as root planned, with cases, assertions\nand deadlines kept. Then run the two commands above, the two owning\nfiles, and gate attempt 3. NF-5 keeps the first gate position.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}